  "body": "Adds a TinyG 3-axis post and generic machine, with expanded drilling, manual tool changes, and named refusals for unsupported operations.\n\nUpdated against main and parent PR #715. The revision fixes tool-change output state and clearance restoration, rejects rounded-zero feeds, handles circles/helices safely, and adds an optional script-level spindle delay. Smoothing requests receive an explanatory comment. XY arcs remain native; other-plane arcs use chords bounded to 0.005 mm including output rounding.\n\nAlso adds the missing grblHAL recorded test suite and its 11 fixtures so the inherited parent post satisfies the shared suite-completeness check. No grblHAL production code is changed by that test addition.\n\nValidation: the full quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`) and app/post all-target clippy passed. The TinyG-focused checks passed 88 tests and app/post clippy with warnings denied. All 19 final TinyG programs passed edge-next host replay using the existing executable recorded from dirty source at `998c02eb`; independent master runtime and physical-board testing are not claimed.\n\nStacked on #715; its changes remain visible until the parent merges. Short-segment simplification and a Setup UI for the script-level spindle delay are outside this PR.\n\nChangelog: Add a TinyG 3-axis post and generic machine with expanded drilling and safe manual tool-change output.\n\nFixes #836\n",
